{"episodes":{"196673":"A prefrontal trough, an approaching tropical wave, and the remnants of Tropical Storm Oscar combined to generate showers and thunderstorms across the area. The diurnal heating and the available moisture from these features also contributed to the development of strong convection across the interior and western Puerto Rico each afternoon. In general, 2 to 3 inches of rainfall were registered each day. This led to urban flooding, as well as mudslides in several municipalities.","196781":"Scattered storms developed along a cold front in northeast Kansas and gradually formed into a line. These storms produced many reports of 55-65 wind gusts and a few instances of small hail up to one inch.","196975":"Isolated thunderstorms developed north of a stationary frontal boundary draped across south-central Illinois during the pre-dawn hours of October 25th.  One cell produced penny-sized hail in Urbana in Champaign County.","197007":"A shortwave moved into Iowa from South Dakota and Nebraska. Convection developed in ahead of, and with the shortwave axis, enhancing later in the evening with the development of the low level jet. ECAPE exceeded 1000 J/kg with effective shear of 30-40+ kts to aid in severe storm development. Additionally, directional shear in the low levels supported rotating updrafts supportive of hail development. Storms across the area produces penny to quarter sized hail with one report up to the size of golf balls.","197463":"During the afternoon hours of October 24th, storms brought widespread damaging wind gusts and a few large hail reports to portions of Missouri.","197469":"During the afternoon and evening hours of October 24th, storms brought widespread damaging wind gusts and a couple hail reports to portions of eastern Kansas.","197576":"A storm system moved east across the area and produced widespread thunderstorms during the evening hours of October 24th. One of these storms become severe as the storm moved into far western Henry County.","197578":"A storm system moved east across the area and led to the development of widespread showers and thunderstorms during the afternoon and evening hours of October 24th. A few of these storms become severe, producing hail up to quarter size and damaging wind gusts. A lightning strike near Keosauqua caused a fire that destroyed a historic church."},"events":[{"begin":"2024-10-25T00:04Z","county":"Caldwell","deaths":0,"end":"2024-10-25T00:05Z","endLat":39.58,"endLon":-94.17,"episode":197463,"id":1221519,"injuries":0,"lat":39.58,"location":"2.96 SSW Mirabile","lon":-94.17,"magnitude":1.0,"narrative":"Mping report of quarter size hail north of Elmira.","source":"Public","state":"MO","type":"Hail","wfo":"EAX"},{"begin":"2024-10-25T00:05Z","county":"Jackson","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-10-25T00:06Z","endLat":39.45,"endLon":-95.8,"episode":196781,"id":1217223,"injuries":0,"lat":39.45,"location":"3 WSW Holton","lon":-95.8,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","narrative":"Gust to 60 mph measured on personal weather station southwest of Holton.","source":"Mesonet","state":"KS","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"TOP"},{"begin":"2024-10-25T00:35Z","county":"Atchison","deaths":0,"end":"2024-10-25T00:36Z","endLat":39.52,"endLon":-95.4,"episode":197469,"id":1221594,"injuries":0,"lat":39.52,"location":"Effingham","lon":-95.4,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Downed trees reported in Effingham.","source":"Emergency Manager","state":"KS","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"EAX"},{"begin":"2024-10-25T00:35Z","county":"Doniphan","deaths":0,"end":"2024-10-25T00:36Z","endLat":39.71,"endLon":-95.26,"episode":197469,"id":1221596,"injuries":0,"lat":39.71,"location":"1.48 SSE Denton","lon":-95.26,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Several tree limbs blown down and minor property damage at a residence near Denton.","source":"Public","state":"KS","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"EAX"},{"begin":"2024-10-2